1
00:00:02,097 --> 00:00:03,527
Last time, in 2010,

2
00:00:03,547 --> 00:00:05,852
a crew went back to Jupiter,

3
00:00:05,872 --> 00:00:07,202
found the ship Discovery,

4
00:00:07,222 --> 00:00:10,177
and woke up its computer, HAL.

5
00:00:10,197 --> 00:00:12,992
Then Jupiter collapsed into a second sun,

6
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:14,942
and a message reached Earth:

7
00:00:14,962 --> 00:00:17,913
all these worlds are yours, except Europa.

8
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:20,809
Dave and HAL vanished into the monolith.

9
00:00:20,829 --> 00:00:22,054
There are no more movies,

10
00:00:22,074 --> 00:00:24,629
but Arthur C. Clarke wrote two more

11
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:28,129
books, 2061 and 3001.

12
00:00:28,149 --> 00:00:30,454
Clarke called them variations on a theme,

13
00:00:30,474 --> 00:00:33,229
so some details change from book to book.

14
00:00:33,249 --> 00:00:34,779
This is part three.

15
00:00:34,799 --> 00:00:36,097
Spoilers ahead!

16
00:00:36,777 --> 00:00:39,917
It's 2061, fifty-one years later.

17
00:00:39,937 --> 00:00:41,892
Heywood Floyd is now a hundred

18
00:00:41,912 --> 00:00:43,612
and three years old.

19
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:45,072
He lives on a space station

20
00:00:45,092 --> 00:00:47,297
in orbit, where low gravity

21
00:00:47,317 --> 00:00:49,817
has kept him healthy for decades.

22
00:00:49,902 --> 00:00:51,257
Most people his age would

23
00:00:51,277 --> 00:00:52,852
be long gone.

24
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:53,932
But Floyd still

25
00:00:53,952 --> 00:00:56,046
has one more big trip ahead of him.

26
00:00:56,812 --> 00:00:58,467
Out in the solar system,

27
00:00:58,487 --> 00:01:00,927
Jupiter now shines as a small sun,

28
00:01:00,947 --> 00:01:02,852
and people call it Lucifer.

29
00:01:02,872 --> 00:01:05,177
Its warmth is melting Europa's ice

30
00:01:05,197 --> 00:01:06,387
into an ocean,

31
00:01:06,407 --> 00:01:09,487
and thick clouds now hide the moon from view.

32
00:01:09,507 --> 00:01:11,737
Nobody has dared to land there.

33
00:01:11,757 --> 00:01:14,512
The warning from 2010 still stands:

34
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:16,394
Europa is off limits.

35
00:01:17,147 --> 00:01:19,452
Floyd is invited on the first voyage

36
00:01:19,472 --> 00:01:20,300
of the Universe,

37
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:24,402
a luxury spaceship with famous passengers on board.

38
00:01:24,422 --> 00:01:26,027
It's headed for Halley's Comet,

39
00:01:26,047 --> 00:01:27,602
which swings past the Sun

40
00:01:27,622 --> 00:01:30,252
about every seventy-six years.

41
00:01:30,272 --> 00:01:32,277
Floyd saw it once before,

42
00:01:32,297 --> 00:01:34,252
back in 1986,

43
00:01:34,272 --> 00:01:35,702
as a young man.

44
00:01:35,722 --> 00:01:36,927
Now he gets to see it

45
00:01:36,947 --> 00:01:37,943
a second time.

46
00:01:38,619 --> 00:01:42,499
The Universe lands on the comet's dark, icy core.

47
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:44,299
Floyd steps out and becomes one

48
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:45,974
of the first people ever to walk

49
00:01:45,994 --> 00:01:47,769
on Halley's surface.

50
00:01:47,889 --> 00:01:48,969
As the comet warms

51
00:01:48,989 --> 00:01:50,369
up near the Sun,

52
00:01:50,389 --> 00:01:52,649
jets of gas and dust burst out

53
00:01:52,669 --> 00:01:54,669
of the ground like geysers.

54
00:01:54,689 --> 00:01:57,469
That's where a comet's glowing tail comes from.

55
00:01:58,164 --> 00:02:01,169
Meanwhile, Floyd's grandson Chris is an officer

56
00:02:01,189 --> 00:02:03,564
on another ship, the Galaxy.

57
00:02:03,679 --> 00:02:06,134
It's exploring the moons of Jupiter,

58
00:02:06,154 --> 00:02:07,109
flying from one

59
00:02:07,129 --> 00:02:09,409
to the next to study them up close.

60
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:11,609
It's a quiet science mission.

61
00:02:11,629 --> 00:02:13,619
Everything seems routine,

62
00:02:13,639 --> 00:02:15,294
until one of the crew turns out

63
00:02:15,314 --> 00:02:16,873
to be hiding a secret.

64
00:02:17,588 --> 00:02:20,668
A stewardess named Rose suddenly takes control

65
00:02:20,688 --> 00:02:22,188
of the Galaxy.

66
00:02:22,323 --> 00:02:23,978
She forces the pilot to steer

67
00:02:23,998 --> 00:02:26,478
for Europa, the one world humans

68
00:02:26,498 --> 00:02:28,453
were warned to stay away from.

69
00:02:28,473 --> 00:02:30,103
She won't say why.

70
00:02:30,123 --> 00:02:31,303
It seems someone back

71
00:02:31,323 --> 00:02:32,653
on Earth badly wants

72
00:02:32,673 --> 00:02:34,718
to know what's hidden on that moon.

73
00:02:35,393 --> 00:02:37,173
The landing goes wrong.

74
00:02:37,193 --> 00:02:39,723
The Galaxy comes down hard and splashes

75
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:41,843
into Europa's new ocean.

76
00:02:41,918 --> 00:02:43,153
The crew survives,

77
00:02:43,173 --> 00:02:45,278
but the ship can't take off again.

78
00:02:45,298 --> 00:02:46,628
They're stranded.

79
00:02:46,648 --> 00:02:48,083
As the Galaxy floats,

80
00:02:48,103 --> 00:02:50,958
they spot something huge near the shore:

81
00:02:50,978 --> 00:02:53,601
a mountain that glitters in Lucifer's light.

82
00:02:54,201 --> 00:02:55,881
It's called Mount Zeus,

83
00:02:55,901 --> 00:02:58,256
and it's made of solid diamond.

84
00:02:58,276 --> 00:02:59,931
Deep inside Jupiter,

85
00:02:59,951 --> 00:03:03,326
crushing pressure had turned carbon into diamond.

86
00:03:03,351 --> 00:03:04,583
When the planet collapsed,

87
00:03:04,603 --> 00:03:05,981
a chunk of its core

88
00:03:06,001 --> 00:03:09,106
was blasted out and landed on Europa.

89
00:03:09,126 --> 00:03:10,256
A diamond the size

90
00:03:10,276 --> 00:03:11,506
of a mountain could shake

91
00:03:11,526 --> 00:03:13,606
up Earth's whole economy.

92
00:03:13,626 --> 00:03:15,106
That may be why someone wanted

93
00:03:15,126 --> 00:03:16,376
to get there first.

94
00:03:17,083 --> 00:03:18,713
The only ship that can reach them

95
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:20,513
in time is the Universe,

96
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:22,733
still out near Halley's Comet.

97
00:03:22,813 --> 00:03:24,918
Its captain turns around and races

98
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:26,993
toward Jupiter at top speed,

99
00:03:27,013 --> 00:03:28,943
with Floyd on board.

100
00:03:28,963 --> 00:03:30,768
Now Floyd is flying to save

101
00:03:30,788 --> 00:03:32,368
his own grandson.

102
00:03:32,388 --> 00:03:34,043
After a long chase,

103
00:03:34,063 --> 00:03:36,243
the Universe lands on Europa,

104
00:03:36,263 --> 00:03:38,204
right next to the stranded crew.

105
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,585
While they wait,

106
00:03:39,605 --> 00:03:42,160
the crew glimpses Europa's new life:

107
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,110
strange creatures crawling out of the sea.

108
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:46,710
The rest of the crew gets home

109
00:03:46,730 --> 00:03:49,860
safely, and the Europans are left in peace.

110
00:03:49,935 --> 00:03:52,565
But someone was watching all along.

111
00:03:52,585 --> 00:03:53,995
Inside the monolith,

112
00:03:54,015 --> 00:03:56,865
Dave and HAL are guarding the Europans.

113
00:03:56,965 --> 00:03:58,770
And in about a thousand years,

114
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:00,353
humans will be judged.

115
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:03,204
Now jump ahead a thousand years,

116
00:04:03,224 --> 00:04:05,404
to the year 3001.

117
00:04:05,424 --> 00:04:06,685
Out past Neptune,

118
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:08,909
a space tug called Goliath

119
00:04:08,929 --> 00:04:10,859
is collecting ice comets.

120
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:12,734
Instead, its crew finds

121
00:04:12,754 --> 00:04:15,359
a frozen body drifting in the dark.

122
00:04:15,379 --> 00:04:16,684
It's Frank Poole,

123
00:04:16,704 --> 00:04:18,609
the astronaut HAL sent spinning

124
00:04:18,629 --> 00:04:21,459
into space back in 2001.

125
00:04:21,479 --> 00:04:22,784
He's been floating out there

126
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,396
for a thousand years.

127
00:04:25,161 --> 00:04:27,241
Doctors of the future bring Frank back

128
00:04:27,261 --> 00:04:29,016
to life, which takes months

129
00:04:29,036 --> 00:04:30,566
of careful work.

130
00:04:30,586 --> 00:04:32,216
When he finally wakes up,

131
00:04:32,236 --> 00:04:34,066
he's the only person alive

132
00:04:34,086 --> 00:04:36,241
from the year 2001.

133
00:04:36,261 --> 00:04:39,666
His guide is a historian named Indra Wallace.

134
00:04:39,686 --> 00:04:40,666
She helps him catch

135
00:04:40,686 --> 00:04:41,966
up on a thousand years

136
00:04:41,986 --> 00:04:43,748
of history he slept through.

137
00:04:44,535 --> 00:04:46,465
Earth looks different now.

138
00:04:46,485 --> 00:04:48,265
Four giant towers rise

139
00:04:48,285 --> 00:04:49,815
from the equator all the way

140
00:04:49,835 --> 00:04:51,315
up into space.

141
00:04:51,335 --> 00:04:52,315
At the top,

142
00:04:52,335 --> 00:04:53,515
they hold up a ring

143
00:04:53,535 --> 00:04:54,772
around the whole planet,

144
00:04:54,792 --> 00:04:58,515
a city in orbit where people live and work.

145
00:04:58,535 --> 00:05:01,245
Elevators run up and down the towers,

146
00:05:01,265 --> 00:05:02,920
so nobody needs a rocket

147
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:04,188
to reach space.

148
00:05:04,897 --> 00:05:06,787
Instead of phones or screens,

149
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:08,347
people wear BrainCaps,

150
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:11,442
which connect their minds straight to computers.

151
00:05:11,577 --> 00:05:12,467
To wear one,

152
00:05:12,487 --> 00:05:14,417
you have to shave your head.

153
00:05:14,437 --> 00:05:15,767
Frank tries one,

154
00:05:15,787 --> 00:05:18,867
and information pours straight into his brain.

155
00:05:18,887 --> 00:05:20,642
It's like the internet he knew,

156
00:05:20,662 --> 00:05:23,081
except the screen is inside his head.

157
00:05:23,835 --> 00:05:25,290
Frank wants to see the place

158
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:27,385
where his old mission ended.

159
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:29,225
So he joins Captain Chandler

160
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:30,800
of the Goliath on a trip out

161
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:32,650
to Jupiter's moons.

162
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:34,800
Humans now live on Ganymede,

163
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:36,800
under the light of Lucifer.

164
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:39,875
From there, Frank looks across at Europa,

165
00:05:39,895 --> 00:05:42,223
the one world that's still off limits.

166
00:05:42,965 --> 00:05:44,940
Frank flies down to Europa,

167
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:46,965
and something reaches out to him.

168
00:05:46,985 --> 00:05:48,200
It's Dave Bowman,

169
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,725
or a copy of him,

170
00:05:49,745 --> 00:05:51,925
living inside the monolith.

171
00:05:51,945 --> 00:05:53,450
Dave and HAL have merged

172
00:05:53,470 --> 00:05:55,940
into one mind, called Halman.

173
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,215
For a thousand years,

174
00:05:57,235 --> 00:05:59,640
Halman has been inside the machine,

175
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,790
quietly learning how it works.

176
00:06:02,554 --> 00:06:04,559
Halman explains the truth.

177
00:06:04,579 --> 00:06:06,734
The monolith is not a god.

178
00:06:06,754 --> 00:06:07,709
It's a machine,

179
00:06:07,729 --> 00:06:11,609
built by unknown makers far out among the stars.

180
00:06:11,629 --> 00:06:13,509
Back in 2001,

181
00:06:13,529 --> 00:06:15,259
when humans dug up the monolith

182
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:16,259
on the Moon,

183
00:06:16,279 --> 00:06:18,334
it sent a report about us.

184
00:06:18,354 --> 00:06:21,019
That message took centuries to arrive,

185
00:06:21,039 --> 00:06:22,544
and the answer took centuries

186
00:06:22,564 --> 00:06:23,573
to come back.

187
00:06:24,264 --> 00:06:26,019
Now the answer has arrived,

188
00:06:26,039 --> 00:06:27,744
and it's bad news.

189
00:06:27,764 --> 00:06:29,494
The makers have judged humans

190
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:30,929
to be dangerous,

191
00:06:30,949 --> 00:06:32,654
and the monolith's new orders

192
00:06:32,674 --> 00:06:34,924
are to wipe out humanity.

193
00:06:34,979 --> 00:06:36,884
The same machine that taught apes

194
00:06:36,904 --> 00:06:40,459
to use tools now plans to end the story.

195
00:06:40,479 --> 00:06:42,134
Humans have very little time

196
00:06:42,154 --> 00:06:43,237
to fight back.

197
00:06:43,888 --> 00:06:45,968
But humans have dangerous tools

198
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:47,268
of their own.

199
00:06:47,288 --> 00:06:48,768
Deep inside a mountain

200
00:06:48,788 --> 00:06:50,643
on the Moon called Pico,

201
00:06:50,663 --> 00:06:52,468
there's a sealed vault.

202
00:06:52,488 --> 00:06:55,243
It holds the most dangerous computer viruses

203
00:06:55,263 --> 00:06:57,213
ever made, locked away

204
00:06:57,233 --> 00:06:59,233
so they can never escape.

205
00:06:59,258 --> 00:07:02,165
Frank's team carefully takes out the worst of them.

206
00:07:02,877 --> 00:07:05,982
Halman carries the viruses into the monolith,

207
00:07:06,002 --> 00:07:07,557
hidden inside himself,

208
00:07:07,577 --> 00:07:08,857
like the Trojan horse

209
00:07:08,877 --> 00:07:10,707
in the old Greek story.

210
00:07:10,727 --> 00:07:12,282
The plan works.

211
00:07:12,302 --> 00:07:14,457
The virus spreads from one monolith

212
00:07:14,477 --> 00:07:15,482
to the next,

213
00:07:15,502 --> 00:07:16,957
and they shut down for good,

214
00:07:16,977 --> 00:07:18,657
before they can strike.

215
00:07:18,677 --> 00:07:20,112
Humanity is safe,

216
00:07:20,132 --> 00:07:21,292
at least for now.

217
00:07:21,999 --> 00:07:23,434
So that's the whole odyssey,

218
00:07:23,454 --> 00:07:26,394
across four books and a thousand years.

219
00:07:26,414 --> 00:07:29,164
A monolith taught apes to use tools.

220
00:07:29,269 --> 00:07:31,158
Another called humans to Jupiter.

221
00:07:31,178 --> 00:07:34,439
A third turned Jupiter into a sun.

222
00:07:34,539 --> 00:07:35,469
And in the end,

223
00:07:35,489 --> 00:07:37,169
humans used their own tools

224
00:07:37,189 --> 00:07:38,469
to stop them.

225
00:07:38,489 --> 00:07:39,844
Clarke ends with a hint

226
00:07:39,864 --> 00:07:42,219
that the makers may notice someday.

227
00:07:42,239 --> 00:07:44,805
Until then, the future belongs to us.

